{:edb/db-before-t 825 :edb/db-after-t 826 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534138 50 #inst "2026-10-11T17:05:20.909Z" 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186083255 1038 #edb/ref 17592186411858 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186119749 1038 #edb/ref 17592186411868 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186124597 1038 #edb/ref 17592186411870 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186129197 1038 #edb/ref 17592186411866 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186129199 1038 #edb/ref 17592186411863 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186129278 1038 #edb/ref 17592186411857 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186133765 1038 #edb/ref 17592186411853 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186133836 1038 #edb/ref 17592186411861 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186133887 1038 #edb/ref 17592186411864 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186133893 1038 #edb/ref 17592186411859 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186133912 1038 #edb/ref 17592186411852 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186157384 1038 #edb/ref 17592186411851 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186162013 1038 #edb/ref 17592186411856 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186162093 1038 #edb/ref 17592186411867 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186162113 1038 #edb/ref 17592186411871 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186162134 1038 #edb/ref 17592186411854 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186166831 1038 #edb/ref 17592186411872 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186166885 1038 #edb/ref 17592186411860 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186166959 1038 #edb/ref 17592186411855 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186172049 1038 #edb/ref 17592186411862 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186172134 1038 #edb/ref 17592186411873 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186188328 1038 #edb/ref 17592186411869 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186198395 1038 #edb/ref 17592186411874 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186198449 1038 #edb/ref 17592186411865 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186198971 1068 #edb/ref 17592186197696 13194139534138 17592186045417 false] [17592186231590 1068 #edb/ref 17592186230401 13194139534138 17592186045417 false] [17592186231590 1068 #edb/ref 17592186411821 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186231590 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186231590 1071 "Find the solution $y(t)$ given that the Laplace transform of the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(t)+3{y}^{′}(t)+2y(t)={u}_{2}(t),\\,y(0)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=0,\n$$\n\nis given by\n\n$$\n{s}^{2}Y(s)+3sY(s)+2Y(s)=\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s}.\n$$\n\nThe solution is $y(t)=u(t-2)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}-{e}^{-(t-2)}\\,+\\,$\n{{field-1}}\n$).$" 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186231590 1071 "Find the solution $y(t)$ given that the Laplace transform of the initial value problem\n$y^{″}(t) + 3y^{′}(t) + 2y(t) = u_{2}(t), y(0) = 0, y^{′}(0) = 0$,\nis given by\n$s^{2}Y(s) + 3sY(s) + 2Y(s) = \\frac{e^{-2s}}{s}$.The solution is $y(t) = u(t - 2) \\cdot (\\frac{1}{2} - e^{- (t - 2)} +$\n{{field-1}}\n$)$." 13194139534138 17592186045417 false] [17592186231590 1074 "Using the transformed equation, we solve for $Y(s)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}^{2}Y(s)+3sY(s)+2Y(s) & =\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s} \\\\ ({s}^{2}+3s+2)Y(s) & =\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s} \\\\ (s+1)(s+2)Y(s) & =\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s} \\\\ Y(s) & ={e}^{-2s}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s(s+1)(s+2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the inverse transform, we first use partial fraction decomposition on the algebraic part:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{s(s+1)(s+2)}=\\frac{A}{s}+\\frac{B}{s+1}+\\frac{C}{s+2}\n$$\n\nSolving for the constants, we find $A=\\frac{1}{2}$, $B=-1$, and $C=\\frac{1}{2}$, giving:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{s({s}^{2}+3s+2)}=\\frac{1}{2s}-\\frac{1}{s+1}+\\frac{1}{2(s+2)}\n$$\n\nNow, we apply the inverse Laplace transform. Let \n\n$$\nF(s)=\\frac{1}{2s}-\\frac{1}{s+1}+\\frac{1}{2(s+2)},\n$$\n\nthen, we have \n\n$$\nf(t)=\\frac{1}{2}-{e}^{-t}+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2t}.\n$$\n\nAccording to the second shifting theorem, \n\n$$\n{L}^{-1}{{e}^{-as}F(s)}={u}_{a}(t)f(t-a).\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{e}^{-2s}F(s)} \\\\ y(t) & ={u}_{2}(t)\\,f(t-2) \\\\ y(t) & =u(t-2)(\\frac{1}{2}-{e}^{-(t-2)}+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2(t-2)}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186233367 1068 #edb/ref 17592186411832 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186308409 1068 #edb/ref 17592186307812 13194139534138 17592186045417 false] [17592186308409 1068 #edb/ref 17592186307876 13194139534138 17592186045417 false] [17592186308409 1068 #edb/ref 17592186308179 13194139534138 17592186045417 false] [17592186308409 1068 #edb/ref 17592186411819 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186308409 1068 #edb/ref 17592186411824 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186308409 1068 #edb/ref 17592186411835 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186308409 1071 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=2y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below regarding the given decoupled system of linear differential equations." 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186308409 1071 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=2y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below regarding the given decoupled system of linear differential equations.$\\,$\nThe $x$-axis is a {{field-1}} line.\n\n$\\,$\nThe $y$-axis is a {{field-2}} line.\n\n$\\,$\nThe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-3}}." 13194139534138 17592186045417 false] [17592186308522 1071 "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}-y=0,\\,y(1)=-1,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=2\n$$\n\nUse Euler's Method with two steps to approximate $y(2)$ and ${y}^{′}(2).$" 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186308522 1071 "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}-y=0,\\,y(1)=-1,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=2\n$$\n\nUse Euler's Method with two steps to approximate $y(2)$ and ${y}^{′}(2).$\n\n$$\ny(2)≈{{field-1}},\\,{y}^{′}(2)≈{{field-2}}\n$$" 13194139534138 17592186045417 false] [17592186308728 1068 #edb/ref 17592186307721 13194139534138 17592186045417 false] [17592186308728 1068 #edb/ref 17592186307853 13194139534138 17592186045417 false] [17592186308728 1068 #edb/ref 17592186307934 13194139534138 17592186045417 false] [17592186308728 1068 #edb/ref 17592186308142 13194139534138 17592186045417 false] [17592186308728 1068 #edb/ref 17592186411828 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186308728 1068 #edb/ref 17592186411837 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186308728 1068 #edb/ref 17592186411841 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186308728 1068 #edb/ref 17592186411844 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186314869 1071 "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=x+y,\\,y(0)=0\n$$\n\nUse the trapezoidal method with two steps to approximate $y(1)$ and $y(2),$ rounded to two decimal places." 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186314869 1071 "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=x+y,\\,y(0)=0\n$$\n\nUse the trapezoidal method with two steps to approximate $y(1)$ and $y(2),$ rounded to two decimal places.\n\n$$\n-3.11\n$$" 13194139534138 17592186045417 false] [17592186396318 1071 "Consider a function $b(t)$ such that its Laplace transform is $L{b(t)}=B(s)$ for $s>{s}_{0}.$ Suppose we wish to find $L{{e}^{t}b(t)}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below." 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186396318 1071 "Consider a function $b(t)$ such that its Laplace transform is $L{b(t)}=B(s)$ for $s>{s}_{0}.$ Suppose we wish to find $L{{e}^{t}b(t)}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.By definition of the Laplace transform, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{t}b(t)}&={\\int}_{0}^{\\infty}{{field-1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\&={\\int}_{0}^{\\infty}{{field-2}}b(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\&={{field-3}}\\quad\\text{for }{{field-4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534138 17592186045417 false] [17592186397263 1071 "Consider the boundary value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+9{\\lambda }^{2}y=0,\\,y(0)=y(\\pi )=0,\\,0\\le x\\le \\pi ,\\,\\lambda \\ge 0.\n$$\n\nFind the parameter values corresponding to the eigenvalues and the associated eigenfunctions of this problem." 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186397263 1071 "Consider the boundary value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+9{\\lambda }^{2}y=0,\\,y(0)=y(\\pi )=0,\\,0\\le x\\le \\pi ,\\,\\lambda \\ge 0.\n$$\n\nFind the parameter values corresponding to the eigenvalues and the associated eigenfunctions of this problem.$\\,$ The eigenvalues correspond to the parameter values ${\\lambda }_{n}=$ {{field-1}}, where $n\\in N.$\n\n$\\,$ The eigenfunctions are ${y}_{n}(x)=$ {{field-2}}, where ${B}_{n}\\in R.$" 13194139534138 17592186045417 false] [17592186411681 1080 "20" 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186411681 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186411681 1083 #uuid "012fa540-5e42-507c-b4d7-4be584a8a37c" 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186411682 1080 "An elliptic cone centered at $(-3,0,1)$" 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186411682 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186411682 1083 #uuid "0171cec4-3060-54fe-b331-7b0cb56feb0e" 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186411683 1080 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186411683 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186411683 1083 #uuid "01e7adac-acae-5277-8fa7-552ad19dbced" 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186411684 1080 "images/9e/9e85303ac91d084f055bce35c874eaaab191a44602ce9223e5fda774b8491183.png" 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186411684 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186411684 1083 #uuid "04fb86e1-67a1-5051-8581-e7df8f55db54" 13194139534138 17592186045417 true] [17592186411685 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5}